    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d494">

                <pb facs="0805" n="795" sameAs="frus:frus1946v10/pg795"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">General Marshall to
                        Colonel Marshall S. Carter
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-06-13">13 June 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>887. With regard to SCALS,<anchor n="61" xml:id="d494-f1"/> Liberty ships flying
                    temporary flag under contract, I think, of Maritime Commission to China
                    Merchants Steam Navigation Company. Please see if this can not be readjusted
                    quickly to release ships to Chinese on basis such as applies to FLC surplus
                    property lots now being delivered to Chinese and put into circulation by them in
                    China by sale, but final price and items to be covered under terms negotiated
                    for general surplus property transfers to Chinese. I want to get SCALS under
                    Chinese flag as quickly as possible.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d494-f1" n="61" xml:id="d494-f1-content">
                <p>Shipping Control Authority Liberty Ships.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
